From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: rock-2: run the SD card at 50 MHz

In UHS SDR104 mode at 100 MHz the SD card gave read errors, and files
on it were corrupted. At 50 MHz (high speed) a 1 GiB write and read
back test passes without errors. Use the safer speed.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
diff -ruN a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3528-rock-2.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3528-rock-2.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3528-rock-2.dtsi	2026-10-23 06:48:11.998810561 +0000
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3528-rock-2.dtsi	2026-10-23 06:48:12.006810634 +0000
@@ -282,8 +282,8 @@
 	cap-mmc-highspeed;
 	cap-sd-highspeed;
 	disable-wp;
-	max-frequency = <100000000>;
-	sd-uhs-sdr104;
+	/* SDR104 at 100 MHz gave read errors and file corruption */
+	max-frequency = <50000000>;
 	vmmc-supply = <&vcc_3v3>;
 	vqmmc-supply = <&vccio_sd>;
 	status = "okay";
